/A 2946 0 R
/Alt (The diagram shows a deep learning architecture with three main components: Backbone, Neck, and Head. The Backbone on the left has six stacked blue rectangular blocks labelled Level 1 to Level 6, with Level 6 outlined in red. Yellow arrows indicate data flow from an Input SAR image at the bottom left, through the Backbone, to the Neck. The Neck component in the middle has six stacked orange rectangular blocks, with the top and bottom blocks outlined in red. Black arrows connect the Backbone levels to corresponding Neck blocks. The Head component on the right has six stacked green rectangular blocks, with the top and bottom blocks outlined in red. Black arrows connect the Neck blocks to the Head blocks. A yellow arrow from the Head leads to a Loss function block, which has an arrow labelled Only training pointing to it. Below the Head, a dashed box labelled Anchor strategy contains three outlined rectangles. Below this, three stacked blocks are labelled Confidence prediction, Object classification, and Box regression. A Detection result image is shown at the bottom centre, with a light blue bounding box and a dark blue bounding box, both with numeric labels. A legend at the bottom indicates that stacked coloured rectangles represent Feature maps, yellow arrows represent A series of convolution and nonlinear mapping operations, and black arrows represent Transfer.)
/K 4
/P 47 0 R
/Pg 20 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
