1017 0 obj
<<
/A 3036 0 R
/Alt (The line graph shows five precision recall curves. The horizontal axis is Recall, ranging from 0 to 1 in increments of 0.1. The vertical axis is Precision, ranging from 0 to 1 in increments of 0.1. Five distinct lines represent different categories: BS in green, LW in blue, OS in red, RC in magenta, and SI in cyan. The blue line, LW, maintains the highest precision, starting near 1 and gradually decreasing to approximately 0.7 at a recall of 1. The green line, BS, starts near 0.95 precision, stays above 0.9 until a recall of 0.7, then drops sharply to near 0.2 at a recall of 1. The red line, OS, starts near 0.95 precision, stays above 0.9 until a recall of 0.8, then drops sharply to near 0.2 at a recall of 1. The magenta line, RC, starts near 0.95 precision, stays above 0.9 until a recall of 0.6, then drops sharply to near 0.2 at a recall of 1. The cyan line, SI, starts near 0.95 precision, stays above 0.9 until a recall of 0.5, then drops sharply to near 0.2 at a recall of 1. All lines generally show a decreasing trend in precision as recall increases, with varying rates of decline.)
/K 6
/P 47 0 R
/Pg 24 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
endobj
