<<
/A 3142 0 R
/Alt (The grayscale satellite image displays a sea surface with various dark objects detected. A horizontal axis indicates longitude from 60 degrees West to 56 degrees West. A vertical axis indicates latitude from 57 degrees North to 58 degrees North. Several rectangular bounding boxes with text labels and percentage values overlay the image. A large green bounding box on the right side of the image is labelled BS: 77.14 percentage. A large cyan bounding box in the upper-left is labelled LW: 47.66 percentage. Within this cyan box, a text label reads smooth sea ice edge, and another text label reads melt pond. A smaller cyan bounding box in the lower-left is labelled SI: 55.78 percentage. Two blue bounding boxes are present: one in the upper-centre and another in the lower-centre, labelled LW: 82.66 percentage. The image shows swirling patterns across the sea surface.)
/K 7
/P 47 0 R
/Pg 32 0 R
/S /Figure
/Type /StructElem
>>
