/Alt (The two-panel image shows dark object detection results and oil spill segmentation. Panel a displays a radar image with a coastline at the top. Overlaid on the radar image are multiple rectangular bounding boxes. Blue boxes indicate low wind areas, red boxes indicate oil spills, and purple boxes indicate rain cells. Each box has a numerical percentage indicating detection confidence. For example, a blue box is labelled LW: 81.59 percentage, red boxes are labelled OS: 81.04 percentage, OS: 77.12 percentage, OS: 74.18 percentage, and purple boxes are labelled RC: 56.91 percentage, RC: 58.64 percentage, RC: 83.63 percentage, RC: 85.5 percentage, RC: 93.05 percentage. Panel b displays a map of the same coastline with several dark, irregular shapes representing oil spill segmentation results. The total oil spill area is labelled as 60.18 square kilometres.)
